/T (generally good. There was, however, a need for greater clarity in places. A number of candidates, for instance, appeared to confuse the likely effect of a higher disposable income on the total amount of consumer expenditure with the likely effect on the marginal propensity to consume. There was some strong evaluation shown with some particularly interesting discussion on crowding out and crowding in. It was disappointing, however, that a number of candidates lost focus and wrote about how expansionary fiscal policy would not increase output and would cause only inflation when there is full employment.)
