2020 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Some measures designed to increase short run economic growth, for example, rises in state pensions, may only shift the AD curve. A number of measures, however, designed to increase AD may also shift the aggregate supply curve. For example, the prime aim of an interest rate cut may be to encourage consumers to spend more but it may also increase investment. In such a case, the effect on inflation will depend on the relationship between the increase in AD and AS. If AD increases more than AS, the price level will rise but if the increase in AD is matched by an increase in AS, this have no effect on the inflation rate.)
/E (Some measures designed to increase short run economic growth, for example, rises in state pensions, may only shift the AD curve. A number of measures, however, designed to increase AD may also shift the aggregate supply curve. For example, the prime aim of an interest rate cut may be to encourage consumers to spend more but it may also increase investment. In such a case, the effect on inflation will depend on the relationship between the increase in AD and AS. If AD increases more than AS, the price level will rise but if the increase in AD is matched by an increase in AS, this have no effect on the inflation rate.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
