/E (A central bank may lower its interest rate with the specific intention of lowering the exchange rate possibly with the intention of reducing a current account deficit. A reduction in the rate of interest may, however, not result in a fall in the value of a fixed exchange rate. It would be likely to put downward pressure on the value but a government may seek to maintain the value by instructing its central bank to purchase its currency, using reserves of foreign currency.)
